    "canonical_id": "person:Barzillai",
    "editorial_evidence": [
      "Pinned WLC Ezra 2:61 o150020610101 (לָקַח 'had taken'), o150020610152 (יִּקָּרֵא 'was called'); Nehemiah 7:63 o160070630101 and o160070630152. In both verses the priest first named Barzillai marries a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite. Original frozen ACAI person:Barzillai is the Gileadite elder, person:Barzillai.3 the marrying priest; both have independent explicit name records and original word groups.",
      "Clear-Bible/macula-hebrew@47db250bd55d0d8577f2a94fba114ef16c35b23c WLC/lowfat/15-Ezr-002-lowfat.xml and WLC/lowfat/16-Neh-007-lowfat.xml",
      "Frozen ACAI names at icfmp/ACAI@e80a874e8282f996199c595378a3b3b9a43aac22 people/json/Barzillai.json and Barzillai.3.json"
    ],
    "editorial_reason": "Ezra 2:61 and Nehemiah 7:63 distinguish the descendant priest who married a daughter of Barzillai the Gileadite and assumed that family name from Barzillai the Gileadite himself (the older family namesake who supported David). The Hebrew singular verb 'took [a woman]' and passive 'was called [by their name]' refer to the marrying priest, already indexed as person:Barzillai.3, not the historically distinct Gileadite elder in person:Barzillai. The two direct proper-name tokens naming the Gileadite elder and both original verse references remain unchanged.",
    "review_status": "editorially_reviewed",
